class Solution {
  public int duplicateCarriageTotalReceipt(int[] readings) {
    int[] a=readings; List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();
    {int write=0;for(int read=0;read<a.length;read++)if(write==0||a[read]!=a[write-1])a[write++]=a[read];for(int i=0;i<write;i++)out.add(a[i]);}
    int answer=0;for(int x:out)answer+=x;return answer;
  }
}

privateData.editorialMd:
Build distinctSorted

`readings` is already sorted from smallest to largest. Keep only one copy of each number. Put these numbers in `distinctSorted` in sorted order.

Return the answer

Add up every number in `distinctSorted`. Store the sum in `total`. Complete `duplicateCarriageTotalReceipt` so it returns `total`. Return it, do not print it.

Why this works

Each value in `distinctSorted` follows task 1. The later tasks use only those values. Keeping these steps separate helps avoid returning the list when the question asks for one number. Check empty input, one item, repeated values, and the largest allowed input.

Efficiency goal: time O(n); extra memory, including the helper list, O(n). n is the input length. These labels describe how work and memory grow with the input.

